<div id="blog-page" class="page-view">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <h2>Culinary Journal</h2>
      <p>Mastering the foundations of authentic home cooking.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="blog-layout">
      <div class="blog-intro-box">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Cinzel', serif; color:var(--terracotta); margin-bottom:15px; font-size:1.8rem;">Master the Kenyan Kitchen: The Big 5 Essential Spices</h3>
        <p>In a world of complicated recipes and overflowing spice cabinets, we believe in a simpler truth: You don’t need fifty different jars to cook like a pro. You just need the right five.</p><br>
        <p>At Nyumbani Fresh Blends, we’ve stripped away the noise to focus on the "Big 5"—the foundational spices that define the soul of Kenyan cooking. Whether you’re simmering a Sunday Pilau or a quick weekday Githeri, these pure, unadulterated essentials are all you need to transform a meal from basic to brilliant.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="blog-item">
        <h3>1. Ground Ginger (Tangawizi)</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>The Vibe:</strong> Warm, zingy, and energizing.</li><li><strong>The Nyumbani Difference:</strong> Most commercial ginger is fibrous and pale. Ours is deep, potent, and ground from the finest sun-dried roots.</li></ul>
        <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Don’t just save ginger for tea. Add a half-teaspoon to your meat marinades; the natural enzymes help tenderize the beef while adding a signature "kick."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="blog-item">
        <h3>2. Garlic Powder (Kitunguu Saumu)</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>The Vibe:</strong> Savory, pungent, and indispensable.</li><li><strong>The Nyumbani Difference:</strong> No cornstarch fillers here. Just 100% pure garlic that smells like a fresh harvest the moment you open the seal.</li></ul>
        <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> For the perfect Nyama Choma rub at home, mix our garlic powder with a little salt and vegetable oil. It creates a crust that seals in the juices better than fresh cloves.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="blog-item">
        <h3>3. Pure Turmeric (Manjano)</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>The Vibe:</strong> Earthy, golden, and restorative.</li><li><strong>The Nyumbani Difference:</strong> We source turmeric that is rich in natural curcumin, giving it an unmistakable deep golden hue.</li></ul>
        <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Add a pinch to your rice while boiling for a beautiful golden color and a subtle earthy undertone.</p>
